I have a very compute-intensive function for which I am trying the "For" 
function instead of "for".  I have replaced the old loop which works

for (var1 in 1:5){
        for (var3 in 1:5){
                param1  <- var1-3
                param3  <- var3-3
                param2  <- -(param1 + param3)
                compute_intensive_function(param1, param2, param3, other.stuff) 

        }
}

with (in an effort to gain some speed)

For (var1 = 1:5,
        For (var3 = 1:5,{
                param1  <- var1-3
                param3  <- var3-3
                param2  <- -(param1 + param3)
                compute_intensive_function(param1, param2, param3, other.stuff) 

                }
        )
)

The new loop runs very quickly, produces no errors, but it fails to produce any 
output!  It seems that compute_intensive_function isn't getting run at all.  
Any ideas?

Thanks,
David

